      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "UNDER TWENTY TWO (2) has the strongest current form, having gone under by just over half a length at Port Macquarie after a narrow third there when a well-supported favourite. He is proven around 1250m and has already had the measure of COOL AZ ALETTA recently. Leading contender. FANCY SHOULDER (3) appeals as the main danger after a luckless fourth at Beaumont (Newcastle), where she was slow out and held up, following a long-neck second at Port Macquarie. COOL AZ ALETTA (9) has been costly from a win perspective but comes through Class 1 and Class 2 form, had a blocked run last time and rates strongly enough to be dangerous. JEUNETOS (6) returns from a two-month let-up after fading in the run when seventh over 1413m at Taree. Proven in the conditions and goes well at this track and trip.",
